WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.176 --> 00:00:01.897
(slow music)

00:00:01.897 --> 00:00:03.357
- For me, one of the hardest things

00:00:03.357 --> 00:00:05.681
about having a friend incarcerated,

00:00:05.681 --> 00:00:09.789
is the fact that when I want
to talk to him, I can't.

00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:11.572
We're so used to being able to just

00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:15.009
snap a picture and text it to somebody,

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:19.785
We can't share that kind of
information with inmates.

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:22.368
(bright music)

00:00:24.291 --> 00:00:25.458
I am an artist,

00:00:26.402 --> 00:00:30.569
and I'm also the owner and
director of Flip Booked LLC.

00:00:33.439 --> 00:00:34.615
When you're serving a sentence,

00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:38.439
you miss out on a lot of
the day-to-day activities.

00:00:38.439 --> 00:00:40.851
Being able to see a clip of video

00:00:40.851 --> 00:00:43.804
of your family and friends
can make a huge difference.

00:00:43.804 --> 00:00:47.971
But we can't share that kind
of information with inmates.

00:00:49.711 --> 00:00:51.639
The flip books I do take your video

00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:54.359
and turn it into something
tangible that you can hold.

00:00:54.359 --> 00:00:56.895
Basically, four to six
seconds worth is enough

00:00:56.895 --> 00:00:59.159
to make a nice length of flip book.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.303
And when an inmate gets a flip book,

00:01:01.303 --> 00:01:03.871
they can see a brief moment

00:01:03.871 --> 00:01:07.121
into the lives of the people they love.

00:01:08.391 --> 00:01:10.807
You can say a lot in
thirty sheets of flip book.

00:01:10.807 --> 00:01:12.224
It’s, it’s really cool.

00:01:17.757 --> 00:01:20.311
- I've been incarcerated
in the state of Colorado

00:01:20.311 --> 00:01:21.894
for about 13 years.

00:01:23.942 --> 00:01:26.911
The hardest part of doing
time is being separated

00:01:26.911 --> 00:01:29.185
from the people you care about.

00:01:29.185 --> 00:01:30.943
They said they were gonna send me a gift,

00:01:30.943 --> 00:01:33.014
and I didn't know what it was gonna be.

00:01:33.014 --> 00:01:36.667
And I got a sheet of all
these little pictures,

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.639
and then I understood what it was.

00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:41.282
This was the first one.

00:01:41.282 --> 00:01:44.703
It was a little dog playing in the mud.

00:01:44.703 --> 00:01:46.081
Dog joy.

00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:48.414
Pure, unadulterated dog joy.

00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:53.671
It was a treat, to be able
to sort of get a video.

00:01:53.671 --> 00:01:55.254
You know, in a way.

00:01:58.535 --> 00:02:00.189
- I think it's easy to understand

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:04.578
why flip books can be so
powerful for the inmates.

00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:07.694
But sometimes I feel
like it might almost be

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:11.525
more powerful for the families involved.

00:02:11.525 --> 00:02:14.018
Being able to take just a few seconds

00:02:14.018 --> 00:02:15.154
to capture some video

00:02:15.154 --> 00:02:17.218
that you know is going to end up

00:02:17.218 --> 00:02:19.494
in the hands of the person you love

00:02:19.494 --> 00:02:21.577
is a very powerful thing.

